# Effect Size

## Effect Size

Effect sizes provide ways to estimate the magnitude of an effect

::: subpoint
○ Standardized, so we can compare differences across scales
:::

::: fragment
Cohen's $d$: measure of difference (not a test)

::: subpoint
○ Transforms to the *z*-scale, can interpret in standard deviation units
:::
:::


## Cohen's *d*

:::: {.columns}
::: {.column width="28%"}
#### One Sample

$$ d = \frac{\bar{x} - \mu_0}{s_x} $$


::: {style="font-size:85%}

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
mu_cty <- 30

cty_bar <- mean(mpg$cty)
cty_sd <- sd(mpg$cty)

(cty_bar - mu_cty) / cty_sd
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
[1] -3.087686
```


:::
:::

:::
:::

::: {.column width="44%"}
#### Independent Samples

$$ d = \frac{\bar{x}_1 - \bar{x}_2}{s_p} $$

::: {style="font-size:85%}

::: panel-tabset
### Pull Data

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
four_cyl <- mpg |>
  filter(cyl == 4) |>
  pull(hwy)
eight_cyl <- mpg |>
  filter(cyl == 8) |>
  pull(hwy)
```
:::



### Calculate $d$

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
x_bar_four <- mean(four_cyl)
sd_four <- sd(four_cyl)
n_four <- length(four_cyl)
x_bar_eight <- mean(eight_cyl)
sd_eight <- sd(eight_cyl)
n_eight <- length(eight_cyl)

pooled_sd <- sqrt( 
  ((n_four - 1) * sd_four^2 + 
     (n_eight - 1) * sd_eight^2) /
    ((n_four - 1) + (n_eight - 1)) 
)
(x_bar_four - x_bar_eight) / pooled_sd
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
[1] 2.804565
```


:::
:::

:::

:::


:::

::: {.column width="28%"}
#### Paired Sample

$$ d = \frac{\bar{D}}{s_D} $$

::: {style="font-size:85%}

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
differences <- mpg$cty - mpg$hwy

d_bar <- mean(differences)
d_sd <- sd(differences)

d_bar / d_sd
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
[1] -2.908509
```


:::
:::

:::

:::
::::


## Cohen's *d*

:::: {.columns}
::: {.column width="33%"}
#### One Sample

$$ d = \frac{\bar{x} - \mu_0}{s_x} $$


::: {style="font-size:85%}

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
effectsize::cohens_d(mpg$cty, mu = 30)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
Cohen's d |         95% CI
--------------------------
-3.09     | [-3.39, -2.78]

- Deviation from a difference of 30.
```


:::
:::

:::
:::

::: {.column width="33%"}
#### Independent Samples

$$ d = \frac{\bar{x}_1 - \bar{x}_2}{s_p} $$

::: {style="font-size:85%}

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
four_cyl <- mpg |>
  filter(cyl == 4) |>
  pull(hwy)
eight_cyl <- mpg |>
  filter(cyl == 8) |>
  pull(hwy)

effectsize::cohens_d(four_cyl, 
                     eight_cyl)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
Cohen's d |       95% CI
------------------------
2.80      | [2.35, 3.25]

- Estimated using pooled SD.
```


:::
:::

:::


:::

::: {.column width="33%"}
#### Paired Sample

$$ d = \frac{\bar{D}}{s_D} $$

::: {style="font-size:85%}

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
effectsize::cohens_d(mpg$cty, mpg$hwy, 
                     paired = T)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
Cohen's d |         95% CI
--------------------------
-2.91     | [-3.20, -2.61]
```


:::
:::

:::

